5 Conclusions
It is inconvenient for users to use a physical keyboard with a closed HMD worn in a fully immersive VR environment because users often need to remove the HMD to reach a physical keyboard. This research used data gloves and micro-speakers to provide users with a portable VR haptic keyboard, which allows users to type short data or commands while walking around in a fully immersive VR environment. The system uses sensors to measure vibrations from a physical keyboard and uses micro-speakers to create complex vibrations that simulate measured vibrations, using a trained neural network. Using the developed haptic VR keyboard system, users do not need to take off the HMD.
